              ],
              "_key": "k102"
            },
            {
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "From tax year 2026-27, the Income-tax Rules, 2026 extend the 50% limit to Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Pune and Ahmedabad as well. In Priya's case the rent limit is lower anyway, so it would not change her exemption, but it will help many renters in those cities from next year.",
              "_key": "k103"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k104",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k105",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Rows 4 to 6: Deductions From Salary",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k106",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k107",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The standard deduction under section 19 of the Income-tax Act, 2025 (section 16(ia) of the 1961 Act) is ₹50,000 under the old regime and ₹75,000 under the new regime for FY 2025-26. Row 4(c) is professional tax, a state levy deducted from your payslip. In Maharashtra it is ₹2,500 a year. It is deductible only under the old regime.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k108",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k109",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Rows 10 and 11: Chapter VI-A Deductions",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k110",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k111",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "These are deductions you proved to HR with documents. Priya's are typical for an old-regime salaried taxpayer:",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k112",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k113",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Section 123 (section 80C), ₹1,50,000:",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k114",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " Her own EPF contribution of ₹1,08,000, which is 12% of basic, plus ₹42,000 in an ELSS fund bought through Zerodha Coin. The cap is ₹1,50,000.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k115",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k116",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Section 80CCD(1B), ₹50,000:",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k117",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " Her own NPS contribution, over and above the ₹1,50,000 limit.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k118",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k119",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Section 126 (section 80D), ₹22,800:",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k120",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " Health insurance premium for herself, within the ₹25,000 limit for individuals below 60.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "bullet",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k121",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k122",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Employer contributions to NPS go in row 10(f) under section 80CCD(2). That is one of the very few Chapter VI-A deductions the new regime also allows.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k123",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k124",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Rows 12 to 19: From Taxable Income to Tax",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
