                  "_key": "k165",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Part B is not binding on you. Under the old regime, you can claim an exemption or deduction in your return that is missing from Part B, as long as you are eligible and keep the proof, such as rent receipts, the landlord's PAN if annual rent exceeds ₹1 lakh, and premium receipts. The catch is that your return will then show a refund or a lower tax than Form 16, and processing will compare the two. Expect questions if you cannot back up the claim.",
